#AUTO 95
#NEEDED 1
# eMMC EXT_CSD dump — step 1 of the fast-storage path (issue 110j).
#
# Before switching the eMMC into HS200 (200 MHz, 8-bit), confirm the card
# actually advertises that mode — you don't put a card into a mode it
# doesn't support. This reads the card's 512-byte EXT_CSD (Extended
# Card-Specific Data, its capability + config table) and decodes the
# fields that matter:
#   DEVICE_TYPE[196]  - supported speed modes; bit 4 = HS200 @ 1.8V
#   HS_TIMING[185]    - current timing mode (0 = legacy)
#   BUS_WIDTH[183]    - current data-bus width (0 = 1-bit)
#   EXT_CSD_REV[192]  - eMMC spec revision the card implements
# Plus a bonus for the eMMC-overwrite step (110b, which USB flashing
# builds on): where the boot partition lives and how big it is
#   PARTITION_CONFIG[179], BOOT_SIZE_MULT[226]
#
# Read-only and safe. The read is emmc_read_ext_csd in src/012-emmc.c,
# invoked via the emmc_ext_csd CALL target. Watch for
# "HS200 @ 1.8V SUPPORTED".

CALL emmc_init
CALL emmc_ext_csd
